{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_25538c552f3878ae615d221edd846149ace30af01bb64214206f486a68242d29"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A context chooser feature lets users pick files or folders through a UI to keep them in the assistant's context."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2c7151b184a1d1a8390710945e747d658e5996ceba4919b5a7a2f8fe825dea07"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A code change plan feature lets users describe desired changes, and the AI generates an implementation plan."},{"claim_ids":["clm_67392580d7ca360b63f418f6574123e1b3abd6d93f03e64805d59e1ee25c2bf6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README states the extension adheres to VS Code extension guidelines and best practices, linking to the official Extension Guidelines."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6aba38520ebb75c0e89b51d79621a7ff986b6ad069c3c2902c402934bc632445"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README's changelog section documents an initial release described as including basic chat, change plan, and file explorer functionalities."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a028a2cdf148d13da8dbde7a9de61866ac4a4752c9e45f22c089b12a98afe817"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is a VS Code extension that integrates a coding assistant directly into the VS Code environment."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a1d94b47e859cc83fef3dcea720ad5b4637fb969c9ff099002b0ea8bbe13a94c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The extension requires an API key for either Gemini or OpenAI, with the user prompted to enter the key on first use."}],"claim_ids":["clm_25538c552f3878ae615d221edd846149ace30af01bb64214206f486a68242d29","clm_2c7151b184a1d1a8390710945e747d658e5996ceba4919b5a7a2f8fe825dea07","clm_67392580d7ca360b63f418f6574123e1b3abd6d93f03e64805d59e1ee25c2bf6","clm_6aba38520ebb75c0e89b51d79621a7ff986b6ad069c3c2902c402934bc632445","clm_a028a2cdf148d13da8dbde7a9de61866ac4a4752c9e45f22c089b12a98afe817","clm_a1d94b47e859cc83fef3dcea720ad5b4637fb969c9ff099002b0ea8bbe13a94c"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:19: